 "readme": "# Privacy Preserving XAI\nSource code for reproducing the experiments in [Towards Integration of Privacy Enhancing Technologies in Explainable AI](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.knosys.2025.115235) published in Elsevier Knowledge Based Systems.\n\n## Dependencies\n`innvestigate==2.1.2`, `shap==0.42.1`,`lime==0.2.0.1`, `quantus==0.5.3`,`sdv==1.10.0`,`numpy==1.23.5`, `pandas==1.5.3`,  `scikit-learn==1.2.0`,   `tensorflow==2.14.0`, `tensorflow-privacy==0.8.12`,`keras==2.14.0`\n\n## Datasets and Target Models\nThe `./datasets` folder contains the raw data files of the Adult, Credit, Compas and Hospital datasets used in the experiments. \nThe synthetic datasets using CTGAN, TVAE and Gaussian Copula methods can be generated using `SynDataGen_SDV` notebook.\nThe following notebooks can be used to generate the respective target models:\n1. `BaselineNN` notebook to generate the non-private baseline neural networks.\n2. `SynNN` notebook for models trained on synthetic data.\n3. `DPNN` notebook for models trained with differential privacy.  \n\n## XAI Methods\nThe following notebooks can be used to generate the respective XAI outputs:\n1. `GradientExpl` for integrated gradients and SmoothGrad.\n2. `ShapExpl` for SHAP.\n3. `LimeExpl` for LIME.\n\n## XAI Metrics\n`XAIMetrics` notebook can be used to load the respective models and XAI for computation of faithfulness metrics.\n\n## Post Model Noise\n`PostModelNoise` notebook can be used to add noise to the explanations in the post-model stage.\n\n## Citation\nIf you use the code in this repository, please cite our paper.\n\n```bibtex\n@article{allana2025pets,\n  title={Towards integration of Privacy Enhancing Technologies in Explainable Artificial Intelligence},\n  author={Allana, Sonal and Dara, Rozita and Lin, Xiaodong and Xiong, Pulei},\n  journal={Knowledge-Based Systems},\n  pages={115235},\n  year={2025},\n  publisher={Elsevier}\n}\n```",
